## FEATURES (context)
A. New tool "Select" (toolbar). Two gestures, both ADDITIVE:
   - TAP near a stroke (within ~28px) toggles that stroke in the selection. Tap on empty space clears the selection.
   - DRAG draws a freehand lasso; strokes with at least one point inside the lasso are added.
   Selected strokes turn accent color (#4a3fd0) and a bounding box is shown.
B. Transform (contextual ActionBar, only when tool = Select): Move / Rotate / Scale toggle buttons.
   While one is active and the selection is not empty, DRAGGING on the canvas transforms the selection with a live preview.
   - Move: translate in the camera view plane. Rotate: horizontal drag = around world Y, vertical drag = around camera right axis
     (pivot = selection bounds center). Scale: drag up = bigger, drag down = smaller (uniform, also scales stroke thickness).
   One gesture = ONE undo step.
C. Duplicate (in place, copies become the selection), Duplicate Symmetric (mirror across X=0 plane), Delete, Deselect.
D. Mirrored strokes (mirror=true) are "baked" when transformed: original and its twin become two independent strokes (mirror=false).

DESIGN NOTES
- All edits to strokes go through ONE generic command `ReplaceStrokesCommand(before[], after[])`:
  do() removes every `before` id then adds every `after`; undo() removes every `after` id then adds every `before`.
- Selection lives in `StrokeLayer` (a Set of ids). `layer.remove()` automatically drops an id from the selection.
- Live preview during a transform = setting `group.matrix` on the selected stroke groups (no mesh rebuild). On release the matrix is
  baked into stroke data and committed via the command.

