## ACCEPTANCE TESTS (manual, on tablet)
1. Select tool: tap a stroke -> it turns purple, a bounding box appears, ActionBar shows "1 selected". Tap it again -> deselected. Tap empty space -> selection cleared.
2. Drag a lasso around several strokes -> dashed lasso visible while dragging; those strokes are added to the selection.
3. Move: toggle Move, drag -> live preview; release. One Undo returns everything to the original position; Redo reapplies.
4. Rotate and Scale behave the same (Scale also changes line thickness). Selecting nothing disables the buttons.
5. Mirror stroke (draw with Mirror on) -> Move it: both halves move together. After release they are two independent strokes; one Undo restores the original single mirrored stroke.
6. Dup: copies appear in place and become the selection (turn purple); Move drags them away. Sym: copies mirrored across X=0.
7. Del removes the selection; Undo restores it.
8. Switching to the Brush tool clears the selection (no purple strokes left).
9. With Move active and a stylus seen, finger orbit still works (fingers navigate, stylus transforms).
10. Save, Clear strokes, Open: transformed/duplicated strokes persist. Old 0.6-0.9 files still load.

